The V3D\ file format provides a portable, compressed representation for
interactive 3D vector graphics generated by the
\TeX-aware vector graphics language Asymptote.  It replaces the legacy
PRC format, which was limited to Adobe Acrobat and lacked support for
transparency, B\'ezier patches with vertex-dependent colors,
and B\'ezier triangle patches.
V3D\ content can be embedded in \acro{PDF} files, viewed with an
Okular plugin on \GNU/Linux, or displayed online through a JavaScript-based
viewer.  We describe the format's features, demonstrate its capabilities
through examples, and discuss its role in the ongoing modernization of
Asymptote's rendering pipeline.
